],[67.9,-230.2,1022.5],[70.0,-222.6,1024.7],[69.8,-214.6,1027.5],[66.2,-207.5,1030.4],[64.2,-199.8,1033.3],[58.9,-193.9,1036.0],[55.8,-186.6,1039.7],[55.2,-179.3,1043.1],[54.4,-171.9,1046.6],[54.7,-164.5,1050.0],[56.0,-157.0,1053.6],[55.1,-149.6,1057.5],[54.2,-142.3,1061.5],[54.9,-134.8,1065.3],[55.9,-127.4,1069.7],[58.4,-119.8,1073.9],[60.9,-112.2,1078.1],[63.5,-104.6,1082.3],[66.0,-97.0,1086.2],[65.1,-89.7,1090.8],[64.2,-82.3,1095.4],[64.9,-74.9,1099.6],[65.9,-67.4,1103.9],[68.4,-59.8,1108.0],[70.9,-52.2,1112.0],[73.5,-44.6,1116.1],[76.0,-37.0,1120.2],[75.1,-29.7,1125.1],[73.7,-22.4,1130.1],[70.1,-15.2,1135.5],[64.9,-10.0,1140.4],[59.8,-4.6,1145.3],[56.2,2.6,1150.8],[52.6,9.8,1155.9],[45.7,13.0,1160.1],[37.9,12.2,1163.1],[30.5,9.2,1165.2],[23.6,5.1,1166.7],[16.7,1.0,1168.7],[10.7,-4.3,1170.5]],"mapped_n":1,"km":0.41,"mapped_km":0.0,"traced_km":0.41,"climb_m":168},"buildings":[],"streams":[],"facts":{"drive_km":0.6,"drive_start_m":916,"drive_end_m":995,"drive_climb_m":79,"drive_max_grade_pct":20,"drive_minutes_at_9kmh":4,"walk_km":0.41,"walk_mapped_km":0.0,"walk_traced_km":0.41,"walk_climb_m":168,"box_km":[3.0,2.99],"arrival_m":1173},"edits":["A bench up to 24 m wide is cut along the jeep track to its smoothed profile (the 30 m DSM includes tree canopy).","Road bumps and ruts in the drive are illustrative; the grade and the line of the jeep track are real.","Trees, shrubs, grass tufts and boulders are placed where WorldCover maps that cover; their size and number are illustrative.","The walking loop is a 40 m circle around the arrival point; it is not a mapped trail.","Trees within 70 m of the Raja Gira Castle are left out so it can be seen; WorldCover 2021 maps tree cover there.","The ruin's outline is the OSM fort area (historic=archaeological_site, 'Raja Gira Fort', way 889059633): a narrow spur about 90 m long and 35 m wide, its north end toward the road.","The walls follow that outline as grey schist dry-stone walls 1.6 to 4.5 m high, with gaps where the stone has fallen. The heights and gaps are estimated from the Commons photos, not surveyed.","Round towers stand at the corners and on the east side, about 3 to 4.5 m high (estimated from the photos of the curved bastions).","Rectangular room foundations about 0.9 m high lie inside the walls. Their places and sizes are estimated from the photo of the rooms on the cliff (photo 01).","The great stair at the north end is in photo 06, so its existence is sourced. Its width, length and step count are estimated.","No terrace is levelled: the walls and stair sit on the Copernicus DEM slope (30 m cells), so the wall tops are their height above the ground under them.","The trailhead is the end of the Odigram road (OSM), about 300 m north of the castle. The walk climbs the slope with no mapped footpath, so the route is traced over the DEM. The mosque on the slope below is not drawn here.","The walk from the end of the jeep track follows the mapped OSM footpath for 0.0 km; the last 0.41 km is not mapped and is traced over the ground (easiest slope on the DEM).","Season colours, snow, ice and dawn mist are illustrative.","Traffic on the drive is illustrative: the vehicle kinds are those seen on Swat roads (Willys jeeps, Hilux, Suzuki vans, Mehran cars, CD70 motorbikes, Qingqi rickshaws, painted trucks); their number and movement are not counted."],"sources":[{"name":"Copernicus DEM GLO-30","use":"terrain heights","licence":"© DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018, provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA","url":"https://spacedata.copernicus.eu/collections/copernicus-digital-elevation-model"},{"name":"ESA WorldCover 10 m 2021 v200","use":"trees, meadow, rock, snow","licence":"CC BY 4.0, © ESA WorldCover project 2021","url":"https://esa-worldcover.org"},{"name":"OpenStreetMap: way 889059633 (Raja Gira Fort) and way 546635490 (Odigram road)","use":"the fort outline, the road and its end point","licence":"ODbL 1.0","url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/889059633"},{"name":"Commons photos 01-06 by TANK RAIDER (CC BY-SA 3.0) and Fazal.Khaliq (CC BY-SA 4.0)","use":"wall courses and towers, the stair, the room foundations (heights estimated)","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0 / CC BY-SA 4.0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raja_Gira_Castle.jpg"},{"name":"OpenStreetMap","use":"the Odigram village road to its end north of the castle, the fort outline (Raja Gira Fort) and the mosque footprint","licence":"ODbL, © OpenStreetMap contributors","url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright"}]}